<!--
# Wasm: a beet program running in the browser

Serves a page that boots the wasm `beet` binary with a launch of its own: the
page's `<Wasm src repo main>` names the served repo store and the entry within
it, the browser process resolves and builds that entry exactly as the native
binary does its `--main`, runs it headless, and `<RenderConsole>` renders its
console output. Honors `?color-scheme=dark`.

Install a wasm binary once, then serve:

    just build-wasm-min                  # assets/wasm/beet-min.wasm, what `/` mounts
    beet --main=examples/wasm --watch    # then open http://127.0.0.1:8337

The pages walk the artifact range, which is the whole point of the split: `/`
boots `beet-min.wasm` (`web_min`, the smallest binary that is still a beet
runtime, so its entry sticks to the core vocabulary), `/render` boots
`beet-render.wasm` (`web_render`, the render middle: a wgpu scene in the tab, so
`just build-wasm-render` first), and `/scripting` boots `beet-full.wasm`
(`web_full`, the kitchen sink, so `just build-wasm-full` first). Any
`examples/action/*.bsx` runs off the full binary: point a page's `<Wasm repo
main>` at eg `repo="/examples/action" main="malenia.bsx"`. The entry roots at
the workspace (`<RepoRoot>`), so `<AssetsDir>` serves the examples the browser
reads as its repo and `--watch` live-reloads the browser on any edit under them.

`<RoutesDir>` serves examples/wasm/routes (the pages); `<AssetsDir>` mounts the
workspace assets (the wasm binaries) at /assets and the examples tree at /examples.
The server owns the boot (`CallOnReady` calls it with the process request the
moment the entry loads) and the router is its dispatch child.
-->
<HttpServer {CallOnReady}>
<Router>
	<RepoRoot src="../.."/>
	<PackageConfig title="Beet Wasm" description="A headless beet program running in the browser"/>
	<Theme color={Srgba(Srgba{red:0.0, green:0.8, blue:0.6, alpha:1.0})}/>
	<!-- the whole document tracks the scheme: surface bg + on-surface text, bound to
	     the material role tokens so ?color-scheme=dark recolors the page, not just
	     the console panel. -->
	<Rule tag="html" background-color="@token:Surface" color="@token:OnSurface"/>
	<DefaultAppRoutes/>
	<RoutesDir src="examples/wasm/routes"/>
	<!-- the workspace assets at /assets (the wasm/js binary the page boots), and the
	     examples tree at /examples, the repo store a page's `<Wasm repo="/examples/..">`
	     names, read over http. -->
	<AssetsDir src="assets" prefix="assets"/>
	<AssetsDir src="examples" prefix="examples"/>
</Router>
</HttpServer>
